 getting Howard ticket  sales it's been amazing for us to have  been able to sell out eight shows in  under an hour  when we put tickets on sale a couple of  weeks ago was something that really  shattered my expectations but one of the  really cool things is that both of the  shows that we are doing to you know  obviously to start our weekend has  this it's for the frontline workers  first responders health care heroes so  those first two shows have been free but  the other ones are obviously for the  general public what's really cool is  that thanks to our partnership with  Safeway Canada 100% of our proceeds go  straight to the food banks here in  Alberta that way we can do a lot of good  and raise a lot of money for a cause and  an organization that really needs it  well for sure just give us quickly Brett  a sense of how your community your  province has been coping with the  pandemic what are some of the stories  you've heard from people well Canadians  in general are very tough here in my  province of Alberta we've definitely  been hit by tough times but I know we're  all trying to look for the silver lining  in this and that's why I wanted to do  this concert to raise spirit for  Albertans as well as do it as we've now  announced that we've got three sold-out  shows in Regina Saskatchewan next  weekend so maybe this thing might  snowball into a few more shows in a few  more places do you think this might be  the way of the future Brett that others  will start copying you you know what I'm  not sure if this is the way of the  future it's kind of the way of the  present right now this is the best that  we can do to bring people together and  bring live music back but as far as I'm  concerned I hope we get back to regular  scheduled programming and we get an  opportunity to play that the real shows  the real way that we want you know  hopefully very soon  [Music]
 

